      "message": "[warning] Line 139: 🟡 `hasPermission` uses `default` branches in the `switch (permission)` blocks. That prevents compiler exhaustiveness checks when new `Permission` values are added, so new permissions can be silently denied without any review-time signal. Keep deny-by-default, but remove `default` in inner switches and add an explicit fallback after the switch (or a helper with `static_assert`/`unreachable`) so enum growth is caught at compile time.",
